      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T17:49:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If it\u0027s hard to think of a good name, it probably means there\u0027s something wrong.\nThinking about it, I think the problem is that you have a function that does 2 things, which makes naming harder; and in general a function should do one thing.\nThe solution would be to expose 2 functions.\n- One to check the prefixes - which you already have, validate_client_vm_dice_chain_prefix_match. The client can call that directly instead of having ClientVmDiceChain do so for it. \n- One to validate the signatures \u0026 parse the DICE chain into a ClientVmDiceChain. validate_signatures_and_parse_dice_chain?",
      "parentUuid": "db6349bf_760c7e8c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 48,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 48,
        "endChar": 16
      },
