        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T12:37:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "They aren\u0027t payloads, and that\u0027s a little confusing.\nNodes or certificates. (I think Andrew prefers certificates these days, although the first entry isn\u0027t one.)\n\nI know formally they are the payload inside the cert, but I really don\u0027t think that helps - since we use thew term payload for lots of other things.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "0b7295df65e93f3373993516ad90b3ebd7bd4940",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e64b1498_d1d6ad5b",
        "filename": "service_vm/requests/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T14:23:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The term \"payload\" is derived from the name \"DiceChainEntryPayload\" mentioned in the RKP doc [1] that is maintained by several people working on DICE. What about keeping \"payloads\" here and renaming the struct as \"DiceChainEntryPayload\" in this vector to align precisely with the doc?\n\nIn addition, I named all the places that refer to the `CoseSign1` that wraps the payload \"entry\" to be consistent with \"DiceChainEntry\" in [1].\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/interfaces/security/rkp/aidl/android/hardware/security/keymint/generateCertificateRequestV2.cddl;l\u003d90;drc\u003d8cbbc15bc367183e739989086d52f81637ee475f",
      "parentUuid": "ab40a286_6e5e12d2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "0b7295df65e93f3373993516ad90b3ebd7bd4940",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "393e221e_c79058d1",
        "filename": "service_vm/requests/src/dice.rs",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 63,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T14:38:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, I know, but it\u0027s still a very confusing term in our context, since we use payload to mean the code running in the VM (which is described by a DiceChainEntryPayload).\n\nYou can use DiceChainEntryPayload, although I think CertPayload would be fine. (It\u0027s not exactly the same thing as DCEP since we\u0027ve decoded it a bit.)\n\nBut I really don\u0027t like the use of payload in the variable names etc because of the inherent ambiguity. entry, node_data, cert_details, ... ?",
      "parentUuid": "e64b1498_d1d6ad5b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 63,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 63,
        "endChar": 24
      },
      "revId": "0b7295df65e93f3373993516ad90b3ebd7bd4940",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
