      "writtenOn": "2023-11-29T16:50:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e we use payload to mean the code running in the VM ...\n\nAbsolutely! It seems that \"payload\" has become a victim of its own success (pvmfw also used \"payload\" to indicate the loaded kernel).\n\nRegarding \"node,\" Andrew already suggested to avoid using it previously.",
      "parentUuid": "393e221e_c79058d1",
